      ],
      "fit": 0.75
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The archipelago's power system, operating on a thin operating margin, confronted a critical failure at its frontier power source. Authorities responded with innovative grid stabilization methods to prevent a total generation shortfall. However, the sequence of generator outages highlighted the delicate balance, where a single equipment failure at the frontier can cascade into widespread instability and risk.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Explorer",
